{"repositoryId":719047710,"availability":"available","full":"ceems-dev/ceems","name":"ceems","description":"A Prometheus exporter and a REST API server to export metrics of compute units of resource managers like SLURM, LSF, Openstack, k8s","category":"Developer tools","language":"C","stars":77,"forks":11,"created":"2023-11-15T10:40:30Z","updated":"2026-10-15T13:17:09Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ceems-dev.github.io/ceems/","topics":["cloud","containers","dashboards","ebpf","emissions","energy-monitor","grafana","green-computing","hpc","kubernetes","lsf","metrics-visualization","monitoring","observability","openstack","performance-monitoring","prometheus","prometheus-exporter","slurm"],"demo":"https://ceems-demo.myaddr.tools/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:34.364Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:34.364Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:34.364Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:34.364Z","stars":77,"forks":11}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Compute Energy & Emissions Monitoring Stack (CEEMS) (pronounced as kiːms) contains a Prometheus exporter to export metrics of compute instance units and a REST API server that serves the metadata and aggregated metrics of each compute unit. Optionally, it includes a TSDB load balancer that supports basic access control on TSDB so that one user cannot access metrics of another user.","\"Compute Unit\" in the current context has a wider scope. It can be a batch job in HPC, a VM in cloud, a pod in k8s, etc. The main objective of the repository is to quantify the energy consumed and estimate emissions by each \"compute unit\". The repository itself does not provide any frontend apps to show dashboards and it is meant to use along with Grafana and Prometheus to show statistics to users.","Although CEEMS was born out of a need to monitor energy and carbon footprint of compute workloads, it supports monitoring performance metrics as well. In addition, it leverages eBPF framework to monitor IO and network metrics in a resource manager agnostic way. It also supports eBPF based zero instrumentation continuous profiling of compute units."],"features":["Monitors energy, performance, IO and network metrics for different types of resource","managers (SLURM, LSF, Openstack, k8s)","Supports different energy sources like RAPL, HWMON, Cray's PM Counters and BMC via IPMI or Redfish","Supports NVIDIA (MIG, time sharing, MPS and vGPU) and AMD GPUs (Partition like CPX, QPX, TPX, DPX)","and also supports Dynamic MIG offered by k8s DRA for NVIDIA GPUs."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ceems-dev/ceems/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e363001e3552c63920d81eb7df3130f14242d6f9866bd2c39d38e709c6f5dbac","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:34.520Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:34.520Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Compute Energy & Emissions Monitoring Stack (CEEMS) (pronounced as kiːms) contains a Prometheus exporter to export metrics of compute instance units and a REST API server that serves the metadata and aggregated metrics of each compute unit. Optionally, it includes a TSDB load balancer that supports basic access control on TSDB so that one user cannot access metrics of another user.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ceems-dev/ceems/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"e363001e3552c63920d81eb7df3130f14242d6f9866bd2c39d38e709c6f5dbac","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ceems-dev/ceems/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:34.520Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T13:17:09Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ceems-dev/ceems/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:34.521Z","hash":"e363001e3552c63920d81eb7df3130f14242d6f9866bd2c39d38e709c6f5dbac","originalBytes":21035,"storedBytes":21035,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["ceems","bedrock","metrics","usage","energy","comput